.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Vt EVP_KEYMGMT
is a method object that represents key management implementations for
different cryptographic algorithms.
This method object provides functionality to have providers import key
material from the outside, as well as export key material to the
outside.
Most of the functionality can only be used internally and has no public
interface, this object is simply passed into other functions when
needed.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_fetch
looks for an algorithm within the provider that has been loaded into the
.Vt OSSL_LIB_CTX
given by
.Fa ctx ,
having the name given by
.Fa algorithm
and the properties given by
.Fa properties .
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_up_ref
increments the reference count for the given
.Vt EVP_KEYMGMT
.Fa keymgmt .
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_free
decrements the reference count for the given
.Vt EVP_KEYMGMT
.Fa keymgmt ,
and when the count reaches zero, frees it.
If the argument is NULL, nothing is done.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_get0_provider
returns the provider that has this particular implementation.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_is_a
checks if
.Fa keymgmt
is an implementation of an algorithm that's identifiable with
.Fa name .
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_get0_name
returns the algorithm name from the provided implementation for the
given
.Fa keymgmt .
Note that the
.Fa keymgmt
may have multiple synonyms associated with it.
In this case the first name from the algorithm definition is returned.
Ownership of the returned string is retained by the
.Fa keymgmt
object and should not be freed by the caller.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_names_do_all
traverses all names for the
.Fa keymgmt ,
and calls
.Em fn
with each name and
.Fa data .
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_get0_description
returns a description of the
.Fa keymgmt ,
meant for display and human consumption.
The description is at the discretion of the
.Fa keymgmt
implementation.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_do_all_provided
traverses all key keymgmt implementations by all activated providers in
the library context
.Fa libctx ,
and for each of the implementations, calls
.Em fn
with the implementation method and
.Fa data
as arguments.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_gettable_params
and
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_settable_params
return a constant
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3
array that describes the names and types of key parameters that can be
retrieved or set.
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_gettable_params
is used by
.Xr EVP_PKEY_gettable_params 3 .
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_gen_gettable_params
and
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_gen_settable_params
return a constant
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3
array that describes the names and types of key generation parameters
that can be retrieved or set via
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_get_params 3
or
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_set_params 3
respectively.
.Sh NOTES
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_fetch
may be called implicitly by other fetching functions, using the same
library context and properties.
Any other API that uses keys will typically do this.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_fetch
returns a pointer to the key management implementation represented by an
EVP_KEYMGMT object, or NULL on error.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_up_ref
returns 1 on success, or 0 on error.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_names_do_all
returns 1 if the callback was called for all names.
A return value of 0 means that the callback was not called for any
names.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_free
doesn't return any value.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_get0_provider
returns a pointer to a provider object, or NULL on error.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_is_a
returns 1 of
.Fa keymgmt
was identifiable, otherwise 0.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_get0_name
returns the algorithm name, or NULL on error.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_get0_description
returns a pointer to a description, or NULL if there isn't one.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_gettable_params ,
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_settable_params ,
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_gen_gettable_params
and
.Fn EVP_KEYMGMT_gen_settable_params
return a constant
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3
array or NULL on error.
